<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1756">1756</a>–<a href="/years/1791">1791</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a composer born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1781 and became one of the greatest figures of the Viennese Classical style. A child prodigy who toured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, he wrote over 600 works, including the operas The Marriage of Figaro, Don Giovanni and The Magic Flute, symphonies, piano concertos and chamber music. He died in Vienna at the age of thirty-five, leaving his Requiem unfinished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart.jpg" alt="Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Nepomuk della Croce · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Mozart_Family_-_Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart_headshot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
